/target
# .cargo/config.toml is committed — it carries the wasm getrandom backend flag the
# (oxrdf-dependent) wasm build needs, including on CI.
/dist-node
# Both the host wasm and the lazy XSLT module wasm (+ their JS bindings) are now
# CI-generated — the host from this repo, the module from the ikigai-xslt-module repo
# (cloned + built in pages.yml). Only the hand-written xslt-loader.js glue is committed.
/dist/*.js
!/dist/xslt-loader.js
!/dist/jsonld-loader.js
!/dist/shacl-loader.js
/dist/*.wasm
/dist/*.d.ts
# Cargo.lock IS committed. This repo is an end product, not a library — it builds a
# deployed wasm artifact and the ikigai-net-server binary, and is publish = false. While
# it was lockless every build resolved fresh, so a sibling's publish moved the ground
# under it with no bisectable moment: on 2026-08-12 four crates published and CI went red
# on two OTHER crates that had been stranded for weeks (PR #48). Sibling drift is `just
# drift`'s job, deliberately; it should not arrive inside an unrelated contributor's PR.
.DS_Store
*~
*.swp
*~undo-tree~
/.claude/
